{"seq":3,"slug":"vlm-alignment-rlhf","title":"VLM 对齐与偏好","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/vision-language-models/training/vlm-alignment-rlhf","wordCount":1669,"readingTime":7,"html":"<h1 id=\"vlm-对齐与偏好\">VLM 对齐与偏好</h1><p>一个指令微调后的 VLM 看着一张只有两只猫的照片，被问「图里有几只狗」，会自信满满地答「有三只狗，分布在画面左侧」——它在编造图里根本不存在的东西。这种「答得流畅却不忠于图像」的毛病，监督微调治不好，因为监督损失只会让模型模仿标准答案，无法告诉它「忠于图像的回答比编造的回答更好」。偏好对齐补上这一课：用成对的「更优/更差」回答训练模型，把它对齐到忠实、有用、无害。本篇讲 VLM 偏好对齐为何比纯文本更棘手、RLHF-V 与 DPO 在视觉上的落地、以及用 AI 反馈降低成本的 RLAIF-V。它接续 <a href=\"visual-instruction-tuning\">视觉指令微调</a> 留下的「答得好还差一步」。</p>\n<h2 id=\"核心概念-从模仿到偏好\">核心概念：从模仿到偏好</h2><p>监督微调和偏好对齐的根本差异在于优化的东西不同。监督微调最小化「模型回答」与「标准回答」的差距，是绝对的模仿；偏好对齐最大化「优回答」相对「劣回答」的偏好概率，是相对的比较。对 VLM，最朴素的偏好目标是 DPO 形式：</p>\n<div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">L</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo fence=\"true\">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><mi>I</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><mi>I</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><mi>I</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><mi>I</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo fence=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo fence=\"true\">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{L}_{\\text{DPO}} = -\\mathbb{E}_{(I, q, y_w, y_l)} \\left[ \\log \\sigma\\left( \\beta \\log \\frac{\\pi_\\theta(y_w \\mid I, q)}{\\pi_{\\text{ref}}(y_w \\mid I, q)} - \\beta \\log \\frac{\\pi_\\theta(y_l \\mid I, q)}{\\pi_{\\text{ref}}(y_l \\mid I, q)} \\right) \\right]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">DPO</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:2.4em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">E</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3448em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5198em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1645em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.357em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.143em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3448em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.3488em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1512em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3